cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "prag-platform: a Parametric RAG platform"
message: "If you reference this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Nabi
    family-names: Baloch
    email: nabibuksh.baloch01@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/NabiBukhsh-AI/prag-platform"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-03"
abstract: >-
  A platform that answers queries by composing three classes of knowledge and routing between
  them per query: knowledge already encoded in a model's weights, knowledge injected into
  weights at inference time as retrieved low-rank parameter deltas, and knowledge injected into
  the context window as retrieved text. Parametric knowledge is treated as a tiered, retrievable
  store rather than a static fine-tune, and is gated by an eligibility function because
  parameters are uncitable, unrevocable, and unfilterable per request. The request path is a
  deterministic typed state graph rather than an agent loop.
keywords:
  - parametric RAG
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - low-rank adaptation
  - knowledge fusion
  - grounding
  - multi-tenancy
